member.summary:
Returns true if the finalization is suppressed for an object (the user program called
). The behavior of this function is undefined if the object itself
is not finalizable.

Host-supplied symbol resolver. Set via ;
ClrMD's COM data-target wrapper forwards ICLRSymbolProvider calls here.
Implementations must be thread-safe.

Internal limits. The public API intentionally hides these for now;
the values are conservative defaults that bound CPU and memory while
parsing arbitrarily large or malformed stress logs.

Bitmask of logging facilities the runtime was configured to record
(the runtime's facilitiesToLog). In-process logs only;
 for memory-mapped logs.

Maximum logging verbosity level the runtime was configured to record
(the runtime's levelToLog). In-process logs only;
 for memory-mapped logs.

Current number of allocated stress log chunks across all threads
(the runtime's totalChunk). In-process logs only;
 for memory-mapped logs.
